    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1d13715a53e7b4b6f72abf2ad0ed04a2207ef42df5826421b8195aa529956ddb",
      "text": "Day 6 · In the morning, a short boat ride to the Uros Islands, the famous floating islands made entirely of totora reeds, the same material the islanders use to build their boats and which they even eat. Although fishing remains important, tourism and handicrafts are today a major source of income. After the excursion, tourist bus from Puno to Copacabana, on the Bolivian shore of the lake, and on to La Paz, where your driver meets you for the transfer to the hotel.",
